From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 16:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ax630c: count boots in a reset-surviving register

`bootcount` had nowhere to live on this board. Patch 0020 stopped U-Boot
reading its environment off the eMMC -- the read is 2048 single-block
transfers before the boot has done anything, and one of them timing out
is not recoverable -- and CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV needs a writable
environment. So the counter was inert: `bootlimit` was set, `altbootcmd`
was written, and `bootcount_load()` returned 0 forever.

DM_BOOTCOUNT_SYSCON is the backend for exactly this situation, and this
SoC has the register it wants. TOP_CHIPMODE_GLB_BACKUP1 (0x02390030) is
a 32-bit scratch word in the always-on chipmode block:

  * The BootROM, the first-stage loader and TF-A leave it alone. The only
    code anywhere in the vendor SDK that names it is a get/set pair in
    bl1/board/board.c (get_boot_time/set_boot_time) that NOTHING calls --
    grep the whole tree.
  * It survives a warm reboot and a chip reset, like its neighbour
    BACKUP0 at +0x24 -- the A/B slot and boot-milestone register this
    port already uses as its evidence channel -- and clears on power
    loss, which is the right lifetime for a boot counter.
  * It is a whole word, so the driver's four-byte mode fits: magic 0xB001
    in bits 31..16, count in bits 15..0. BACKUP0 could not host it; its
    low bits are the vendor slot field and 28..31 are this port's
    milestones.

The counter is always armed. There is no `upgrade_available` gate the
way CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV has one, because that gate existed to avoid
writing the environment on every boot and a register write costs
nothing. Every boot increments; a boot that reaches a healthy system
clears it from Linux with one 32-bit write of 0xB0010000 to the same
address. Three failures in a row and the fourth attempt takes
`altbootcmd`, which boots the last generation that cleared the counter.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
--- a/arch/arm/dts/ax630c.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/ax630c.dtsi
@@ -59,6 +59,31 @@
 		value = <0x1>;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The boot counter, in TOP_CHIPMODE_GLB_BACKUP1 (0x02390030 -- the
+	 * chipmode block + 0x30). A 32-bit scratch word that survives a warm
+	 * reboot and a chip reset and clears on power loss, which is exactly
+	 * the lifetime a boot counter wants. Nothing else in the boot chain
+	 * writes it.
+	 *
+	 * `reg` is two entries in the root's 2/2 cells: the register within
+	 * the syscon (offset 0x30, four bytes) and the counter's position
+	 * inside that register (offset 0, four bytes). With a four-byte
+	 * value the driver keeps CONFIG_SYS_BOOTCOUNT_MAGIC's top half in
+	 * bits 31..16 and the count in bits 15..0, so a cleared counter
+	 * reads 0xB0010000 and Linux clears it with one 32-bit write.
+	 *
+	 * /chosen/u-boot,bootcount-device is not set: this is the only
+	 * UCLASS_BOOTCOUNT device in the tree, so it is the one found.
+	 */
+	bootcount: bootcount {
+		compatible = "u-boot,bootcount-syscon";
+		syscon = <&chipmode_syscon>;
+		reg = <0x0 0x30 0x0 0x4>,
+		      <0x0 0x00 0x0 0x4>;
+		reg-names = "syscon_reg", "offset";
+	};
+
 	soc {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 		#address-cells = <2>;
@@ -175,6 +200,18 @@
 		};
 
 		/*
+		 * TOP_CHIPMODE_GLB. +0x24 is the A/B slot and boot-milestone
+		 * register this port already writes with `mw.l` from the
+		 * environment; +0x30 is the boot counter below. Both are
+		 * scratch words the ROM, the first-stage loader and TF-A
+		 * leave alone.
+		 */
+		chipmode_syscon: syscon@2390000 {
+			compatible = "syscon", "simple-mfd";
+			reg = <0x0 0x2390000 0x0 0x1000>;
+		};
+
+		/*
 		 * uart0 is the boot console on hidden pads; uart1 is on an
 		 * exposed header pin but is not muxed to it by firmware and
 		 * has never been shown to work on this board. 208 MHz is the

--- a/arch/arm/dts/ax630c-nanokvm-pro-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/ax630c-nanokvm-pro-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -20,3 +20,11 @@
 &common_syscon {
 	bootph-all;
 };
+
+&chipmode_syscon {
+	bootph-all;
+};
+
+&bootcount {
+	bootph-all;
+};

--- a/configs/ax630c_nanokvm_pro_defconfig
+++ b/configs/ax630c_nanokvm_pro_defconfig
@@ -32,7 +32,8 @@
 # CONFIG_EFI_PARTITION is not set
 CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
-CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_DM_BOOTCOUNT=y
+CONFIG_DM_BOOTCOUNT_SYSCON=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD="mw.l ${msreg_set} ${ms_altboot}; run bootfallback || run bootfallback || run bootfallback || run bootfallback; mw.l ${msreg_set} ${ms_failed}; reset"
 CONFIG_DM_REGULATOR=y

